WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.791
The fictional prototype is accurate, but missing approved access blocks the affected pilot.

00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:07.573
The manager pauses it.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:11.137
Nobody borrows another account to meet the deadline.

00:00:11.137 --> 00:00:16.482
The policy owner addresses the access dependency through the approved human process.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:24.946
Now justify the decision: accuracy does not resolve access or accountability, and simulated support does not show actual acceptance.

00:00:24.946 --> 00:00:27.173
Then revise conditions that matter.

00:00:27.173 --> 00:00:34.301
Change the message from start now to the pilot is paused while approved access is resolved.

00:00:34.301 --> 00:00:42.319
Change the support resource so the first step checks permitted access and points to the coordinator for questions.

00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:44.546
Retain review and stop duties.

00:00:44.546 --> 00:00:50.783
Restart depends on the appropriate human decision after access, permission and support are verified.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:55.237
Record the old condition, revised condition, evidence and expected effect.

00:00:55.237 --> 00:00:58.801
An expected improvement is not an observed result.
